📥 Setup & Installation Guide
1. Arduino Firmware Setup
Open the Arduino IDE.

Ensure you have the built-in Keyboard library installed.

Open arduino-firmware/LeonardoController.ino.

Select your board (Arduino Leonardo) and correct port under Tools > Board.

Upload the code to your Arduino. (Note: Unplug the HC-05 TX pin temporarily while uploading code over USB if you run into serial conflict upload errors).

2. Android App Setup
Open Android Studio.

Select Open and choose the android-app/ directory.

Allow Gradle to sync dependencies.

Build and install the application onto your Android device (supports Android 12+ Bluetooth permissions automatically).

💡 Usage
Power on your hardware system.

Open the Android application and press CONNECT HC-05 to establish serial pairing.

Tap any workflow card to execute the target HID sequence, or use the manual switches at the bottom to control states.
